# fleet-ops#9605 (Nish said yes on 2026-10-12, see that issue): the two
# automated reviewers approve worker code (.py, .sh, bin/, scripts/). New
# scripts are still refused by the `ci` check (.semgrep/no-glue.yml), and any
# edit under .github/ needs both automated reviews (config/risky-paths.json
# "guard"). Nish's review stays on the files below: the safety rules and their
# scanners, the tests that prove the agent jail, deny lists, the units that
# confine agents, seat keys and credentials. Public repos refuse push rulesets,
# so this uses CODEOWNERS + require_code_owner_review.
#
# Tier B moved to the veto window (fleet-ops#9605 follow-up): root-run host
# config that does not confine the agents (the sysctl hardening file, the audit
# rules, ansible/host.yml and ansible/update.yml, and the systemd units named in
# "veto_window" in config/risky-paths.json) merges by itself 24 hours after the
# reviewers approve, unless Nish vetoes (a comment starting with "veto", or the
# label nish-veto). Tier A stays here because these files are the checks on the
# agents themselves: an agent-run pipeline must never approve a change to the
# rules that judge it, to the sandbox it runs in, or to the keys it could use.
# A new unit under rootfs/etc/systemd/system/ is tier A until it is named in the
# unowned exceptions below AND in "veto_window".

# The merge guard and its review prompt.
/config/risky-paths.json @nish3451
/prompts/risky-review.md @nish3451
# The no-glue rule and the secret and private-detail scanners, with their ignore files.
/.semgrep/ @nish3451
/.semgrepignore @nish3451
/.gitleaksignore @nish3451
/.github/gitleaks-private-detail.toml @nish3451
# Tests that prove the worker jail hides every login and that App tokens are minted safely.
/tests/test_claude_lanes.py @nish3451
/tests/github_app_stub.py @nish3451
# Agent deny lists and permission policy.
/rootfs/etc/claude-code/ @nish3451
# Root-run host config that confines the agents or the network: firewall,
# privilege, and every unit that sandboxes or limits an agent, a runner or its
# login (agent.slice, claude.slice, actions.runner.*, hermes-*/sandbox.conf,
# anything with Sandbox, Protect*, ReadOnlyPaths, InaccessiblePaths, User= or
# CapabilityBoundingSet, the user-1000 slice limits, the Claude login directory).
/rootfs/etc/nftables.conf @nish3451
/rootfs/etc/polkit-1/ @nish3451
/rootfs/etc/systemd/system/ @nish3451
# Tier B units: a path with no owner has none, and the last matching line wins.
/rootfs/etc/systemd/system/fleet-host-config.service
/rootfs/etc/systemd/system/fleet-host-config.timer
/rootfs/etc/systemd/system/fleet-update.service
/rootfs/etc/systemd/system/fleet-update.timer
/rootfs/etc/systemd/system/fleet-unit-failed@.service
/rootfs/etc/systemd/system/restic-r2-backup.service.d/10-size-guard.conf
/rootfs/etc/systemd/system/restic-r2-locked-copy.service.d/10-needs-backup.conf
/rootfs/etc/systemd/system/tailscaled.service.d/50-restart-always.conf
/rootfs/etc/systemd/system/session-.scope.d/50-interactive-cpu-priority.conf
/rootfs/etc/systemd/system/system.slice.d/50-memory-protect.conf
/rootfs/etc/systemd/system/hermes-gateway.service.d/60-clean-sigterm.conf
/rootfs/etc/systemd/system/hermes-gateway.service.d/70-oom-protect.conf
/rootfs/etc/systemd/system/claude-remote-control.service.d/50-alert-on-stop.conf
/rootfs/etc/systemd/system/claude-remote-control.service.d/selfheal.conf
# Seat keys and credentials.
/credentials/ @nish3451
**/*seat*.conf @nish3451
*.env @nish3451
# This file.
/.github/CODEOWNERS @nish3451
